IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vmu-s01-purposes`
IMPORT `vmu-s03-definitions`

-- Tests of sections 1 and 3.
-- Each expected value is worked out by hand from the quoted line above it.

§ `Section 1 -- Purposes`

-- Lines 23 to 34 are twelve lines of text: the opening words, six paragraphs (a) to (f) and five subparagraphs (i) to (v) of (d).
-- src:23 | The main purposes of this Act are—
-- src:24 | (a) to provide for fees and penalties to be fixed by reference to fee units or penalty units that can be indexed annually by an amount to be fixed by the Treasurer;
-- src:25 | (b) to change certain penalties that are specified in monetary amounts in certain Acts to penalty units;
-- src:26 | (c) to change certain fees that are specified in monetary amounts in certain Acts to fee units;
-- src:27 | (d) to authorise the Governor in Council to make regulations—
-- src:28 | (i) converting references to fees and penalties in monetary amounts to equivalent fee units and penalty units;
-- src:29 | (ii) converting references to fee units and penalty units to equivalent fees and penalties in monetary amounts;
-- src:30 | (iii) converting existing references to fee units to equivalent fee units under this Act;
-- src:31 | (iv) converting existing references to the monetary value of fee units or penalty units to the equivalent value under this Act;
-- src:32 | (v) increasing fees that have remained in monetary amounts to fee units having regard to the indexation that would have applied if they were in fee units;
-- src:33 | (e) to change penalty units in the Petroleum (Submerged Lands) Act 1982 to monetary amounts;
-- src:34 | (f) to amend the Sentencing Act 1991 and the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994.
#ASSERT count `s 1 -- the main purposes of this Act, as the text prints them` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT at `s 1 -- the main purposes of this Act, as the text prints them` 0 EQUALS "The main purposes of this Act are—"

§ `Section 3 -- Definitions`

-- src:42 | fee includes charge or other amount;
-- "fee includes charge or other amount": each of the three is enough, and a thing that is none of them has no answer.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a fee` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a fee` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a fee` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a fee` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a fee` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- src:44 | instrument maker has the same meaning as in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994;
-- "instrument maker has the same meaning as in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994": the answer is the borrowed fact.
#ASSERT     `s 3 -- the person is an instrument maker` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 3 -- the person is an instrument maker` FALSE

-- src:46 | legislative instrument has the same meaning as in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994;
-- "legislative instrument has the same meaning as in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994".
#ASSERT     `s 3 -- the instrument is a legislative instrument` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 3 -- the instrument is a legislative instrument` FALSE

-- src:47 | penalty means a fine or other monetary penalty and includes an amount payable under an Act or statutory rule in respect of an offence for which an infringement notice can be issued under the Act;
-- "penalty means a fine or other monetary penalty and includes an amount payable under an Act or statutory rule in respect of an offence for which an infringement notice can be issued under the Act".
-- Arguments in order: a fine; another monetary penalty; payable under an Act or statutory rule; in respect of an offence; an infringement notice can be issued under the Act.
-- A fine, or another monetary penalty, is a penalty.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a penalty` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a penalty` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An amount that meets all three facts of the "includes" limb is a penalty although it is neither a fine nor another monetary penalty.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a penalty` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each fact of the "includes" limb is needed: leaving out any one of the three, the item is not a penalty.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a penalty` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a penalty` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a penalty` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Nothing at all: "means" closes the definition, so the answer is JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 3 -- the item is a penalty` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- src:48 | penalty unit has the same meaning as in section 110 of the Sentencing Act 1991;
-- "penalty unit has the same meaning as in section 110 of the Sentencing Act 1991".
#ASSERT     `s 3 -- the thing is a penalty unit` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 3 -- the thing is a penalty unit` FALSE

-- src:49 | statutory rule has the same meaning as in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994.
-- "statutory rule has the same meaning as in the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994".
#ASSERT     `s 3 -- the instrument is a statutory rule` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 3 -- the instrument is a statutory rule` FALSE
